# Miden Drop chain rules

This workspace is exclusively for the Miden Drop bearer note.

## Files

- Contract: `contracts/drop-note/src/drop_note.masm`
- Contract documentation: `contracts/drop-note/README.md`
- Tests: `integration/tests/drop_note_test.rs`

Do not add unrelated account components, binaries, client stores, or generic contract scaffolding
without an explicit product requirement.

## Semantics

- Storage is exactly `[expiration_block]`.
- Zero means no expiration.
- Before expiration, possession of the private note data authorizes the claim.
- At and after expiration, only the note sender may consume it.
- Move assets through the standard Basic Wallet library.
- Treat the exact expiration block as expired.
- Never describe reclaim as automatic.

## Validation

```sh
cargo fmt --manifest-path integration/Cargo.toml -- --check
cargo test -p integration --release
```

The MASM note is compiled by the integration test through `NoteBuilder::code`; it has no separate
contract build command.
